{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>במרכבת המשנה (in the second chariot).</b> The second to his chariot, that goes alongside his — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 41:43). But behold, it is a noun, and so too \"כהני המשנה\" (II Kings 23:4), \"את משנה התורה הזאת\" (Deuteronomy 17:18). The correct interpretation is that משנה is an epithet, like \"ואנכי אהיה לך למשנה\" (I Samuel 23:17), \"כי מרדכי היהודי משנה למלך אחשורוש\" (Esther 10:3), and likewise \"כסף משנה\" (Genesis 43:12) is an epithet, like 'double silver,' and the grammarians (Radak in Sefer haShorashim, root שנה) have already brought proof from the fact that all of these have a segol, while \"משנה התורה\" and all the construct forms have a tsere, according to the rule of the construct state. The matter is that the king has a chariot known to him, as it is stated (Esther 6:8) \"וסוס אשר רכב עליו המלך,\" and another known to his second, and after him for the third:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "Ramban invokes the segol/tsere distinction between the absolute and construct forms of משנה as evidence that the absolute form is an epithet; the hyper-literal rendering preserves his phonological argument."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:43:40.683655754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}